<Positioned left="96" top="1340" width="980"><Container alignment="CENTER_LEFT"><Text fontSize="15" color="#7A6A52FF" fontFamily="Noto Serif CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">Worked from the centre outwards. The kestrel panel is the only motif that uses the shaded B/C range; all other motifs stay inside three shades so the sampler can be stitched from a single thread card.</Text></Container></Positioned>
<Positioned left="96" top="1420"><Text fontSize="13" color="#8A7A62FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">FICTIONAL SAMPLER · pattern, place name and floss numbers are invented for a DSL study; not a commercial chart.</Text></Positioned>
